# About the team and role
  text: The Team: Revenue Operations – Americas
  text: You’ll join a hands-on Revenue Operations team that partners directly with the Americas go-to-market (GTM) organization. The team supports d
  text: This is a collaborative, fast-moving environment where Revenue Operations works alongside sellers and leaders to improve revenue visibility,
  text: Revenue Operations Specialist
  text: The Revenue Operations Specialist is a junior-level individual contributor who partners with GTM teams across the Americas. Reporting to the
  text: You’ll be embedded in day-to-day GTM execution, responding to operational needs while contributing to longer-term improvements in revenue pr
# What you will do
  text: Revenue Reporting & Executive Analytics
  text: Provide day-to-day support to GTM team members with pipeline visibility, deal tracking, and reporting needs.
  text: Build, maintain, and refine operational dashboards and reports used in weekly GTM meetings, forecasting cadences, and executive reviews.
  text: Gather feedback from GTM teams and translate it into practical recommendations that improve sales processes, data quality, and operational e
  text: Sales Process, Forecasting & Day-to-Day GTM Support
  text: Partner with Americas GTM teams on active pipeline management, including opportunity structure, stage progression, data hygiene, and forecas
  text: Provide hands-on guidance on sales processes, opportunity hygiene, and Salesforce usage in support of active deals.
  text: Identify friction in daily execution and help implement improvements to workflows, stage definitions, handoffs, and tools.
  text: Balance timely execution support with longer-term process improvements that help the business scale without slowing delivery.
  text: Technology, Data & Systems Enablement (Americas)
  text: Support testing, training, user readiness, and cutover activities for the planned Salesforce migration across the Americas.
  text: Assist GTM teams use sales tools effectively in their day-to-day work, including Seamless, Salesloft, and Gong.
  text: Collaborate with the Salesforce Center of Excellence on Americas GTM processes, integrations, reporting, and system enhancements.
# What you will do
  text: 2-4 years of experience in Revenue Operations, Sales Operations, Business Operations, or a related role.
  text: Working knowledge of Salesforce, including core objects, relationships, reporting, and how data and automation support GTM processes.
  text: Experience supporting or partnering with sales, customer success, marketing, or other GTM teams in a fast-paced environment.
  text: Experience in a regulated, data-driven, transaction-based, or enterprise software business.
  text: Ability to translate business needs into clear process and reporting recommendations.
  text: Strong communication and collaboration skills, with the confidence to partner across functions and levels.
  text: Curious, self-aware, and eager to learn; able to seek guidance, apply feedback, and transfer learning to new situations.
  text: Organized and detail-oriented, with the ability to manage multiple priorities and follow through on commitments.
  text: Proficiency with Salesforce and common GTM technologies.
  text: Experience creating or maintaining reports and dashboards in Salesforce, Power BI, or a comparable reporting tool.
